          <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-6">
            <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5">
              <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--color-consul);">§ 06 · The parallel agent</span>
              <h2 class="display-lg mt-4">
                Hermes never sleeps.
              </h2>
              <a href="#" class="caption text-ink-subtle mt-4 inline-block">100+ Hermes skills</a>
            </div>
            <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7 body-base text-ink-muted space-y-4 prose">
              <p>
                Hermes is a parallel Python-based agent that runs autonomous and scheduled work while Claude Code handles your interactive sessions. They share your filesystem but operate independently. Useful for background jobs that shouldn't tie up your main session.
              </p>
              <p style="color: var(--color-ink);">
                100+ Hermes skills across Apple ecosystem, autonomous orchestration, creative tooling, data science, DevOps, email, GitHub, MCP scaffolding, media, MLOps, note-taking, productivity, research, smart home, social media, and software development.
              </p>
              <p class="italic">
                Example: <em>"Every weekday at 7am, run my morning brief: yesterday's calendar, today's calendar, overnight inbox, top 3 priorities. Drop it in Obsidian and Slack it to me."</em> Hermes handles the cron. You just receive the brief.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========== WORKFLOWS ========== -->
      <section class="py-20 md:py-24">
